# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# The security headers in firebase.json's `hosting.headers` block have NEVER
# applied in production: this project's frontend ships from Cloudflare Pages
# and the deploy pipeline is pinned to `--only functions,firestore`
# (docs/firebase/deploy.md), so Firebase Hosting - and everything configured
# under it - is never deployed. This file is the Cloudflare-side counterpart,
# the same way frontend/functions/api/session/[[path]].ts is the counterpart of
# that block's `/api/session/*` rewrites.
#
# Vite copies public/ verbatim into dist/, which is the Pages build output, so
# this lands at the deployment root where Pages looks for it.
#
# The directive-by-directive evidence for the CSP below lives in
# .agents/docs/research/browser-ai-csp.md (S1-S7). Two deliberate differences
# from the firebase.json value it is derived from:
#
#   1. GA4 origins are added. src/main.tsx calls startAnalytics(), and
#      src/firebase/analytics.ts loads the Analytics SDK whenever
#      VITE_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID is set - which injects a tag from
#      www.googletagmanager.com and beacons to *.google-analytics.com /
#      *.analytics.google.com. The firebase.json value predates that wiring and
#      would silently kill GA4 on any deployment that configured it. Harmless
#      allowlist entries where no measurement id is set: nothing loads at all.
#      Two more origins belong to the same SDK, not to GA4 itself:
#        - https://firebase.googleapis.com: getAnalytics() fetches
#          /v1alpha/projects/-/apps/<appId>/webConfig to resolve the
#          measurement id dynamically (fetchDynamicConfig). Without it the SDK
#          logs "Failed to fetch this Firebase app's measurement ID" and falls
#          back to the local measurementId, but only after a CSP violation.
#        - https://firebaseinstallations.googleapis.com: @firebase/installations
#          registers a Firebase Installation ID before any event is sent.
#          Blocking it rejects the Analytics bootstrap promise outright
#          ("TypeError: Failed to fetch") and no GA4 events are ever sent.
#   2. `connect-src 'self'` now also covers /api/session/*, which reaches Cloud
#      Functions through the same-origin Pages Function rather than directly.
#
# Not covered here: if this Pages project enables Cloudflare Web Analytics,
# Cloudflare injects a beacon from https://static.cloudflareinsights.com, which
# `script-src` below blocks. Add that origin only if that feature is turned on.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://apis.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https://*.google-analytics.com; connect-src 'self' https://asia-northeast2-teamc-2026.cloudfunctions.net https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com https://securetoken.googleapis.com https://firestore.googleapis.com https://firebase.googleapis.com https://firebaseinstallations.googleapis.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://huggingface.co https://*.hf.co https://raw.githubusercontent.com; worker-src 'self'; frame-src https://teamc-2026.firebaseapp.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
